SQL placed before :PARAMETERS, which the builder discards (style guide
datasource_sql_body_after_parameters, reviewer-enforced; no LSP rule owns
it). Only :DSN forms the header; the misplaced :PARAMETERS sits in the
body, where its inline `:=` is a strong SSL marker (D15: a `:=` anywhere
in the body is decisive; only a header :PARAMETERS has its defaults
excluded). So the document classifies as SSL: SSL diagnostics run, of
which only unknown_token on `@` surfaces (unexpected_token is off in data
sources), and the SQL lines, which do not parse as SSL, are left as
written with no `;` added (issue #351). The :PARAMETERS line between them
belongs to that unterminated run, so no section blank line follows it.
Recorded so a change to how this broken layout classifies is visible.
-- input.ds --
:DSN := DATABASE;
SELECT tag_id, tag_label
FROM asset_tag
:PARAMETERS sLabel := "";
WHERE tag_label = @sLabel
-- format --
:DSN := DATABASE;
SELECT tag_id, tag_label
FROM asset_tag
:PARAMETERS sLabel := "";
WHERE tag_label = @sLabel
-- diagnostics --
5:19-5:20 error unknown_token: Unknown token: '@'
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
5:19-5:20 error unknown_token: Unknown token: '@'
